---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
const faqSchema = faqPageSchema([
  { question: 'Does setup install Ghidra, Hopper, or IDA?', answer: 'REA setup registers MCP and may offer Hopper with approval — Ghidra/IDA stay bring-your-own existing installs. Mythbust for community questions.' },
]);
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Does setup install Ghidra, Hopper, or IDA? | rea.run"
  description="REA setup registers MCP and may offer Hopper with approval — Ghidra/IDA stay bring-your-own existing installs. Mythbust for community questions."
  path="/faq/setup-vs-providers/"
  schema={faqSchema}
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/faq/">← FAQ hub</a></p>
    <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">FAQ · P1</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">Does <code>setup</code> install Ghidra / Hopper / IDA?</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none"><strong>Short answer:</strong> REA does <em>not</em> ship a decompiler. It wires engines you already have (or explicitly approve).</p>

    <h2>What setup actually does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Registers the REA MCP server with your coding agent client.</li>
      <li>May write investigation skills to a skills directory.</li>
      <li>May <strong>offer</strong> to help install or locate <strong>Hopper</strong> depending on host/docs — only with your approval; still not “REA embeds Hopper.”</li>
      <li><strong>Ghidra</strong> and <strong>IDA</strong> are bring-your-own: install them yourself, export paths / MCP config, then <code>doctor --provider …</code>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Mythbust</h2>
    <p>Community explainers put it cleanly: REA “doesn’t ship a decompiler; it wires Hopper/Ghidra you already have” (<a href="https://x.com/cai_smart/status/2108370877448691754" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">@cai_smart</a>). Live user questions from <a href="https://x.com/Thomas3cnl/status/2109195402830573847" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">@Thomas3cnl</a> match this FAQ.</p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/docs/install/">Install guide</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/mcp-clients/">MCP client matrix</a></li>
      <li><a href="/faq/macos-ghidra-decompiler/">macOS Ghidra decompiler</a></li>
      <li><a href="/showcase/rea-ida-adapter/">IDA Free adapter</a></li>
    </ul>

    <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Sources</p>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs">
        <li><a href="https://x.com/cai_smart/status/2108370877448691754" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">@cai_smart — does not ship a decompiler</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://x.com/Thomas3cnl/status/2109195402830573847" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">@Thomas3cnl — setup vs engines Q</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://x.com/Thomas3cnl/status/2108859787752661206" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">@Thomas3cnl — related setup Q</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/installation.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Upstream installation docs</a></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
